# Ambulance & hub context

## Current setup
- Scene: `scenes/units/ambulance.tscn`
- Script: `scripts/units/ambulance.gd`
- Simple circle Node2D; instanced under `MapScene` as `Ambulance`
- Travels with tweens via `move_to(world_pos)` and `return_to_hub()`
- Signals: `arrived_at_target`, `returned_to_hub`

## Hub
- Player will choose the hub cell at run startup (not implemented yet)
- Until then, hub defaults to grid center `(2, 2)`
- `GameManager.hub_cell` + `Ambulance.setup(hub_cell, hub_world_pos)` wire the home position
- Ambulance always returns to that hub after a dispatch

## Intentionally not built yet
- Player picking hub on startup
- Player manually controlling / dispatching the ambulance
- Skill tree (will define automated behavior; mostly auto, optional manual)
- Cure/kill resolution tied to arrival

## When extending
- Keep movement API on `Ambulance` (`move_to`, `return_to_hub`, hub fields)
- Put skill-tree modifiers and dispatch policy outside the node (systems / game manager)
- Do not bury player-input handling inside `ambulance.gd` until that feature is requested
